# ⚡ Shannon (Shannon AI)
> **Autonomous TinyML Compiler & Hardware Optimization Studio**
> *Compressing giant intelligence into micro-scale silicon.*

---

## 🎯 Overview
**Shannon** is an autonomous developer platform and agentic optimization compiler designed for Edge AI and TinyML. Named in honor of **Claude Shannon**, the pioneer of Information Theory and digital compression, this studio takes standard machine learning models (PyTorch, ONNX, TensorFlow) and automatically optimizes, quantizes, and compiles them into zero-dependency, ultra-fast C/C++ firmware headers ready to run on resource-constrained microcontrollers (ESP32-S3, STM32H7, ARM Cortex-M, RISC-V).

---

## 🚀 Key Features
- 🧠 **Agentic Graph Pruning & Quantization:** Autonomous search for the Pareto frontier balancing accuracy vs. SRAM/Flash memory footprint.
- 📊 **3D Memory Arena Profiler:** Visual inspection of layer-by-layer buffer allocation, tensor arena usage, and latency estimates.
- ⚡ **Zero-Dependency C/C++ Codegen:** Generates clean, header-only C/C++ kernels optimized for CMSIS-NN and ESP-NN.
- 🧪 **In-Browser WebAssembly Simulator:** Test quantized model inference live in the browser using webcam or audio feeds before flashing hardware.

---

